Verdict: NOT_SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that the author of 'What is Property?' was a member of a national governing body and inspired a political group founded by George Valois and Georges Sorel. The evidence confirms that the author was Pierre-Joseph Proudhon and that the political group Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel, Charles Maurras, and a selective reading of Proudhon. However, the evidence does not support that Proudhon was a member of a national governing body. Additionally, the claim that Olivier Ferrand was elected to the governing body is not supported by any evidence.
Rounds: 3, findings: 6
Sources:
- Cercle Proudhon: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cercle_Proudhon
